From 6110f93cd74eb6ae91193c7ab3023223e2f2fc08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:39:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add the one settings registry profiles read and write
 through

Without this there is no single surface a profile can snapshot: every profile
switch would need per-setting wiring and any setting added to Forge later would
silently fall outside profiles. The registry derives its descriptors from the
resolved runtime graph, so new rails, gates, phases, adapters and roles are
profileable with no changes here. Writes go through the sparse config writer and
prune values equal to the package default, which is what makes an apply
idempotent and a profile flip leave no residual diff.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
